---
import Meta from "../Meta.astro";
import Stats from "../Stats.astro";
import Sec from "../Sec.astro";
import Figs from "../Figs.astro";
import ProblemSolution from "../ProblemSolution.astro";
---
<Meta rows={[["Role", "UI/UX Designer"], ["Team", "3 Designers, 2 Developers"], ["Timeline", "Aug – Dec 2022"], ["Skills", "UX research, UI design, Marketing, Ideation, Developer hand off"]]} />
<ProblemSolution problem="Lack of value proposition and communication" solution="Clear CTA and better related imagery" />
<p class="lead">UVU's Student Leadership and Success Studies department helps students learn soft skills for their careers, with classes in stress management, speed reading, and leadership.</p>
<p>We found they lacked a website that communicated the value of their degrees and classes. Most students who took their classes enjoyed them, but the department had no way to communicate that value to new students. We found school counselors were the best CTA, and making sure students knew the class numbers was the next most effective way to get them to sign up.</p>
<Sec h="Research and analysis">
  <p>During the discovery phase, we ran research to gather insights and understand user needs. Here are some of our survey results.</p>
  <Stats items={[["52%", "Had never heard of the SLSS department", "Only 7% had learned about it from the website."], ["80%+", "Enjoyed the classes they took"], ["Top 3", "Leadership, stress management, job placement", "What students said mattered most."]]} />
</Sec>
<Sec h="Insights: users didn't know who they are or why they should care">
  <p>From user interviews, questionnaires, and eye tracking, we found the site didn't tell users who the department was or why they should care about its classes.</p>
  <p>Students had often heard of some classes, or even taken them, but didn't know the bigger picture. They tended to take only individual classes that friends or counselors suggested.</p>
  <Figs items={[["eye-tracking.png", "Eye tracking"], ["site-map.png", "Site map"]]} />
</Sec>
<Sec h="Ideating">
  <p>Once we had research insights and a clearer understanding of the requirements, we began designing in Figma. I was in charge of the home page wireframe: a larger header with a clear value proposition, and cards that show off the value of the department's most popular classes.</p>
  <Figs items={[["Wireframe---1.0-Home-Page.png", "Home page wireframe"]]} cols={1} />
</Sec>
<Sec h="Game plan: a better call to action">
  <p>We decided the best CTA was to direct students to the counselors who often suggested these classes. To show off what the department offered, we made cards for the most popular classes, each with a tagline about why you'd want to take it.</p>
  <Figs items={[["home-CTA.png", "Home page CTA"], ["card-anatomy.png", "Card anatomy"]]} />
  <Figs items={[["Shots-create-mockups-5.png", "Final design on a laptop"], ["1.0-Home-Page.jpg", "Full home page"]]} />
</Sec>
<Sec h="Pitch to the stakeholders">
  <p>We presented to the department faculty and left them with all of our research, designs, and ideas in a handoff document. The site is being developed by students at UVU.</p>
  <blockquote class="pull">“Probably my favorite presentation. I really like how you used the data, the design of the site, the rationale, etc. Knocked it out of the park!”<cite>Faculty feedback</cite></blockquote>
</Sec>
<Sec h="Results">
  <Stats items={[["32%", "Improvement to navigation", "Students took less time to get around the page."], ["70%", "Improvement to class selection", "Finding why to take a class improved by over 70%."], ["121%", "Improvement in counselor sign up", "Students found how to book a counselor over twice as fast."]]} />
</Sec>
